    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60569" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύ-ημα</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that
				which is conceived, embryo, foetus</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				7.6
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				461c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				719b33
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in
			Botany, <i>that which is swollen as the result of growth</i>, e.g.
			base of flower-head, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				6.4.3
			</span></i>: of a cabbage-sprout, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.642
			</span></i>.</div>
